  "name": "Pokémon Game Show 2013 Mystery Card Battle",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "The Pokémon Game Show was held at Tokyo Big Sight on 17 and 18 August 2013, where Pokémon X and Y were first playable. Its card tournament, the \"Mystery Card\" Battle, ran each day in a primary school league and an open league. Players brought their own 60-card deck and, at the start, got a sealed \"mystery pack\" of two cards, both Team Flare Grunt, a card not yet released, which had to replace two cards of their deck. Winners got exclusive Pokémon Game Show promos.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: Pokémon Game Show",
        "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_Game_Show"
      },
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: Team Flare Grunt (XY 129)",
        "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Team_Flare_Grunt_(XY_129)"
      }
    ]
  },
